{"agent_id":"pp3g-jlse-validation-task-evidence-only-not-a-system-to-ship","agent_seq":36,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T04:07:17.107569819Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7efd07df-fbdf-492d-a2cc-7754eb5448b4","comment_uuid":"315d402c-0c5f-4443-b3e1-56600a2d5be1","author":"pp3g-jlse-validation-task-evidence-only-not-a-system-to-ship","content":"## Re-Review Verdict: PASS\n\nEvery MUST FIX (1-5) and Also-Fix (A-B) from #199 is verified as correctly applied in revision b40c980. Each item below is independently re-derived from primary artifacts (raw epoch_ms from logs, dist-info METADATA files, initialize-capture.json content).\n\n---\n\n### MUST FIX 1 — Cold-start range (n=3) — **PASS**\n\n**Required:** Replace single 2639 ms figure with full n=3 range; ceiling = observed max 2761.\n\n**Verified:** Report §5 table (line 235) states `2155–2761 (median 2639; observed max 2761)` with n=3 label. §5 finding (lines 255-257) calls out 2761 as the ceiling explicitly: *\"observed maximum 2761 ms — that observed maximum, not any single sample or average, is the value that feeds the cold-start latency ceiling.\"* §7 conclusion (lines 350-352) repeats the range and ceiling. §6 item 5 (line 315) restates 2155–2761 with observed max.\n\n**Independent re-derivation from raw epoch_ms:**\n- Test 2: `tests1-3-harness.log:57` start=1785983153227 end=1785983155866 → **2639 ms** ✓\n- Test 4: `test4-harness.log:22` start=1785983161306 end=1785983163461 → **2155 ms** ✓\n- Test 5: `test5-harness.log:23` start=1785983171102 end=1785983173863 → **2761 ms** ✓\n\nRange 2155–2761, median 2639, max 2761 — all correct.\n\n---\n\n### MUST FIX 2 — Backend-init band (no silent exclusion) — **PASS**\n\n**Required:** Widen or split the backend-init band to include all four logged values.\n\n**Verified:** Report §5 table (lines 238-239) now shows two rows: cold n=3 `1083.0–1345.0` (median 1255.5) and Test 4 respawn n=1 `1573.6`. Lines 244-250 explicitly state the union range `1083.0–1573.6 ms` and explain why the respawn is on its own row (different code path). Line 249: *\"Neither sample is silently excluded: both bands are reported and the union range is stated.\"* §6 item 5 (lines 312-314) and §7 (lines 352-353) repeat the full decomposition.\n\n**Independent re-derivation from proxy logs:**\n- `tests1-3-proxy.log:11` init_ms=**1255.5** (Test 2 cold)\n- `test4-proxy.log:11` init_ms=**1083.0** (Test 4 cold first call)\n- `test4-proxy.log:20` init_ms=**1573.6** (Test 4 respawn — after SIGKILL)\n- `test5-proxy.log:11` init_ms=**1345.0** (Test 5 cold)\n\nCold band: 1083.0–1345.0 ✓. Respawn: 1573.6 ✓. Union: 1083.0–1573.6 ✓. All four accounted for.\n\nProxy spawn range also corrected (§5 line 236): 1028–1390 (n=3, median 1342). Re-derived:\n- Test 2: 1785983154569 − 1785983153227 = **1342 ms** ✓\n- Test 4: 1785983162334 − 1785983161306 = **1028 ms** ✓\n- Test 5: 1785983172492 − 1785983171102 = **1390 ms** ✓\n\n---\n\n### MUST FIX 3 — stdio-only scope + cut untested recommendation — **PASS**\n\n**Required:** (a) Cut or hedge the \"longer-lived transport\" recommendation; (b) add stdio-only scope statement to §7.\n\n**Verified:**\n(a) §6 item 5 (line 317-318): the sentence now ends at *\"the lazy connection defeats it today)\"* — the \"or a longer-lived transport than stdio\" clause is gone. ✓\n(b) §7 caveat (c) (lines 355-358): *\"transport scope: every finding in this report is for stdio transport only — stdio for both the ToolRegistry→proxy hop and the proxy→backend hop. Streamable HTTP, SSE, and websocket transports were not tested, and the conclusion must not be read as covering them.\"* ✓\n\n---\n\n### MUST FIX 4 — listChanged correction + initialize capture — **PASS**\n\n**Required:** (a) Correct claim to \"explicitly declares listChanged: false\"; (b) supplementary initialize-capture.json artifact on file, cited wherever handshake/capability claims are made.\n\n**Verified:**\n(a) Test 5 row (line 201): *\"Its server capabilities explicitly declare tools.listChanged = false\"* with explanation that the SDK serializes the field as false rather than omitting it. ✓\n(b) `logs/initialize-capture.json` exists (171 lines). Contains:\n- `send` entry (line 19-34): raw initialize request with timestamp `2026-08-06T03:31:19.359Z` ✓\n- `recv_raw` entry (line 37-41): raw response with timestamp `2026-08-06T03:31:20.277Z` containing `\"tools\":{\"listChanged\":false}` verbatim ✓\n- `recv_parsed` entry (line 43-63): parsed JSON confirming `listChanged: false` ✓\n- `listChanged_serialization_note` entry (line 65-74): explicit note that `listChanged_present: true`, `listChanged_value: false` ✓\n\nCitations: Test 5 row (line 201) ✓, §3 artifact table (line 81) ✓, §6 item 1a (lines 273-286, substantial detail) ✓, §8 log index (line 370) ✓. No handshake claim is made without the artifact.\n\n---\n\n### MUST FIX 5 — Pinned deps — **PASS**\n\n**Required:** Pin toolregistry==0.15.0 and mcp==2.0.0 in the reproduce block.\n\n**Verified:** §3 reproduce block (line 91): `pip install toolregistry[mcp]==0.15.0 mcp==2.0.0` ✓. Lines 83-87 explain the pin rationale (mcp 2.0-era APIs required).\n\n**Independent verification from installed packages (read-only, dist-info METADATA):**\n- `/tmp/toolregistry-venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/mcp-2.0.0.dist-info/METADATA` line 3: `Version: 2.0.0` ✓\n- `/tmp/toolregistry-venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/toolregistry-0.15.0.dist-info/METADATA` line 3: `Version: 0.15.0` ✓\n\nBoth match the report pins exactly.\n\n---\n\n### Also-Fix A — 15 ms residual reconciliation — **PASS**\n\n**Required:** Account for the 15.5 ms residual in Test 2 decomposition.\n\n**Verified:** Report lines 150-162 now add a \"Post-response tail\" line: the SDK post-call `tools/list` refresh arrives at the proxy at epoch 1785983155864 (13 ms after the `tools/call` response at 1785983155851); the harness records return at 1785983155866 (2 ms later). Total: **15 ms**. Lines 157-158: *\"The columns sum exactly when epoch-derived inter